nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BEast: ^*NIs ^*BCoded 10 Lead^*n played when opponents are in NT contract?|
PG| ***** 41 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Yes coded tens are typically only played in NT contracts.|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|On the line of play, West can count 2 hearts, 2 diamonds, and 1 spade for sure. West then needs two more tricks.|
PG| ***** 43 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|One possibility is to hope I have the @SK which gives Declarer at least one extra trick. And if spades are 3-3 and there are entries to dummy that is a second spade trick.|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So it is possible to make but very unlikely. Most would go down.|
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


