PG| ***** 76 ***** |


mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If East wants to take a bid, we will use |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ogust,Ogust^*N|CP||FP||at|. 3@D possible also but I think 2N |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ogust,Ogust^*N|CP||FP||at| is better.|
PG| ***** 77 ***** |


mb|2N|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|2N is an artificial asking bid. Many play it asks for a ^*BFeature^*n meaning if the Weak-2 opener has an outside A or K he bids it. However, I prefer the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ogust,Ogust^*N|CP||FP||at| that lets you describe two features about your hand simultaneously;
Whether or not you have a ^*BGood Suit^*n meaning 2 of the top 3 honors, and;
Whether or not you have a ^*BGood Hand^*n meaning 8+ points.|
PG| ***** 78 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The responses to 2N are all artificial.
^C3@C = Bad hand Bad suit
^C3@D = Bad hand Good suit
^C3@H = Good hand Bad suit
^C3@S = Good hand Good suit.|
PG| ***** 79 ***** |


mb|P|mb|3H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|On this hand West has a 3@H response (Good hand Bad suit).|
PG| ***** 80 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BA Kib: ^*NShould West open with preempt in 1st seat vulnerable?|
PG| ***** 81 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That is a good question. With 2 aces one could argue 2@S is not correct but not quite strong enough for 1@S.|
PG| ***** 82 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In my style there is no gap between opening 1@S and 2@S. If I have a hand with 6-card suit not strong enough to open 1@S I just about always open 2@S. There are no hands too weak for 1@S and too strong for 2@S.|
PG| ***** 83 ***** |


